        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-29T15:05:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note that we\u0027re not considering the layer\u0027s color space here, but I *think* that\u0027s okay, if we assume that any restore-filtering should be in the original device\u0027s color space? (Because this code path is logically equivalent to \"no rendering happens in the layer, the DAG is evaluated as part of the restore\". Is that right, @michaelludwig@google.com?)",
      "revId": "0c21de5fcd9874c5570433d31fb869630ee0c192",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "11b8b214_b3d226b7",
        "filename": "src/core/SkCanvas.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 1291,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-04T19:51:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is where we need to convey the SaveLayerRec\u0027s color space explicitly, because I think the image filtering should also operate in the layer\u0027s chosen color space.\n\nW/o a source SkDevice to carry that data, and no longer just matching \u0027dst\u0027, we need something else to convey that info. But I think adding a ColorInfo parameter to `internalDrawDeviceWithFilter` will actually help clarify everything because we can be explicit about the choices at each call site instead of relying on magical inference working out by using `dst`\u0027s info.",
      "parentUuid": "edc9433f_d4364d4e",
      "revId": "0c21de5fcd9874c5570433d31fb869630ee0c192",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
